## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 20+
- pnpm 9+
{% if tech_stack.database == 'postgresql' %}- PostgreSQL 15+{% endif %}

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <repository-url>
cd {{ project_name_kebab }}

# Install dependencies
pnpm install

# Set up environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your configuration

{% if tech_stack.database == 'postgresql' %}
# Set up database
pnpm db:generate
pnpm db:push
{% endif %}

# Start development server
pnpm dev
```

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Required |
|----------|-------------|----------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | PostgreSQL connection string | {% if tech_stack.database == 'postgresql' %}Yes{% else %}No{% endif %} |
| `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` | NextAuth.js secret key | Yes |
| `NEXTAUTH_URL` | Application URL | Yes |

## Available Scripts

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `pnpm dev` | Start development server |
| `pnpm build` | Build for production |
| `pnpm start` | Start production server |
| `pnpm lint` | Run ESLint |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Run TypeScript compiler |
| `pnpm test` | Run tests |
| `pnpm db:generate` | Generate database migrations |
| `pnpm db:push` | Push schema to database |
| `pnpm db:migrate` | Run migrations |
| `pnpm db:studio` | Open Prisma Studio |

